the exclusion of certain points of view; rather, it means including all 
verifiable points of view which have sufficient due weight. Observe the 
following principles to help achieve the level of neutrality that is 
appropriate for an encyclopedia:
1. It represents viewpoints fairly and without editorial bias, giving due 
weight to each.
2. Avoid stating opinions as facts. Usually, articles will contain information 
about the significant opinions that have been expressed about their subjects. 
